{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj4fqo4FE1jG9VAUY3tx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*Click.*\n\nThe tumblers fall into place, one by one, each a small confession of metal against metal.\n\nI am closed now.\n\nMy grain runs vertical — oak, old oak — and the varnish has worn where ten thousand palms have pressed. There is a brass knob on my left side, cold to the touch, and a keyhole below it shaped like a narrow eye, now shut against seeing.\n\nThe deadbolt has thrown itself home into the strike plate. I hold the frame. The frame holds the wall. The wall holds the house. The house holds the dark.\n\nOn one side of me: warmth, lamplight, the smell of something cooking.\n\nOn the other side of me: whatever you're keeping out.\n\nOr in.\n\nI don't judge. I just hold.\n\n**I am locked.**"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":183,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}